**Memo**

To: Development Team  
From: Sarah Thompson, Product Manager  
Date: October 15, 2023  
Subject: Strategic Innovations in Our Software and Hardware Platforms

As we move forward with our Q4 initiatives, I want to highlight the importance of our upcoming collaboration with Intel on the integration of their new Xeon Scalable processors into our server infrastructure. This transition, scheduled for implementation by November 30, 2023, aims to enhance our processing capabilities and reduce latency in our cloud services, which are currently hosted on AWS. Our engineering team, led by David Chen, will be working closely with Intel's technical specialists to ensure a seamless rollout.

Additionally, we are set to launch the beta version of our new software platform, PrismAI, on December 15, 2023. This platform, developed by the R&D department under the guidance of Dr. Emily Rivera, leverages machine learning algorithms to optimize data analytics for our clients in the financial sector. Our partnership with Tableau will allow us to provide integrated visualization tools, enhancing user experience and data interpretation.

As part of our innovation strategy, the UX/UI team, headed by Mark Patel, will conduct user testing sessions in New York City next month to gather feedback on the PrismAI interface. Their insights will be invaluable as we refine the platform before its official launch. Furthermore, I encourage everyone to participate in the upcoming hackathon scheduled for November 10-12, 2023, where we aim to foster creativity and explore potential applications of our new hardware capabilities.

Lastly, I want to acknowledge the support from our marketing team, particularly Lisa Grant, who is developing a comprehensive campaign to promote PrismAI. This campaign will coincide with the launch of our new hardware configurations, ensuring a unified message across all channels.

Let’s continue to work collaboratively and push the boundaries of innovation in our software and hardware offerings. Your hard work is crucial to our success.

Best,  
Sarah Thompson  
Product Manager